          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            There are different, related ways in which one could view the notion of
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                algebra over a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
          %ul
            %li
              If one views monads as a generalization of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+theories"} algebraic theories
              (see
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+theory#RelationToMonads"} algebraic theory - relation to monads
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+a+Lawvere+theory"} algebra over a theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operations"} operations
            %li
              From the 2-dimensional point of view, an algebra over a monad is a special case of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+over+a+monad"} module over a monad
              for the bicategory
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+category"} terminal category
            %li
              If one views monads as a way to model computational effects (see
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad+in+computer+science"} monad in computer science
          %p
            Algebras over a monad are usually objects equipped with extra
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/properties"} properties
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+an+endofunctor"} algebras over the underlying endofunctor
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/properties"} properties
          %p
            The corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+duality"} dual
            notion is that of
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coalgebra+over+a+comonad"} coalgebra over a comonad
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
